WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.451 --> 00:00:03.414
(snappy music)

00:00:03.414 --> 00:00:06.721
- Captain's log: 53 days,
and still no sign of a—

00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:08.804
- Captain Cousteau, look!

00:00:10.306 --> 00:00:12.723
- Finally, I seaweed made it.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:14.714
Dock her here.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:17.297
(snappy music)

00:00:18.321 --> 00:00:22.393
Welcome to California's
majestic kelp forest,

00:00:22.393 --> 00:00:24.815
the redwoods of the ocean.

00:00:24.815 --> 00:00:28.065
(quaint, French music)

00:00:36.241 --> 00:00:39.372
Kelp is one of the fastest
growing plants on Earth.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:43.584
Some species can grow
up to 24 inches per day.

00:00:43.584 --> 00:00:46.257
Giant kelp, like the ones around us,

00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:48.757
can reach upwards of 200 feet.

00:00:51.252 --> 00:00:54.941
- That's taller than the
Leaning Tower of Pisa.

00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:56.128
- Exactly.

00:00:56.128 --> 00:00:59.467
Kelp forests thrive in
cool, coastal waters

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:02.297
and are home to hundreds of
different types of animals

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:05.380
like seals, sea lions, lobster, fish,

00:01:06.474 --> 00:01:09.224
sea otters, urchins, even octopi.

00:01:10.827 --> 00:01:15.330
More than just cold water,
kelp likes turbulent water.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.913
(snappy music)

00:01:19.205 --> 00:01:20.059
Thanks.

00:01:20.059 --> 00:01:22.726
(snappy music)

00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:25.875
These turbulent waters are constantly

00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:29.088
stirring up nutrients that
kelp needs to survive.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:32.047
Unfortunately, these forests off Catalina

00:01:32.047 --> 00:01:35.000
are suffering from the
effects of climate change

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.339
and warming ocean temperatures.

00:01:38.339 --> 00:01:41.736
(snappy music)

00:01:41.736 --> 00:01:42.946
Ah.

00:01:42.946 --> 00:01:44.613
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:01:45.728 --> 00:01:48.706
I have an idea, gather around everyone.

00:01:48.706 --> 00:01:51.206
Let's take a kelp-fie, get it?

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:53.428
They don't get it.

00:01:54.824 --> 00:01:57.083
(camera clicks)

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.666
(snappy music)

